48 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="07f80e41-afd3-4e58-8a50-a6b39b64ceb9" data-testid="conversation-turn-46" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="10fda578-c365-459d-8576-92e0fb021bc5" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-instant"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="52">Good question ⚡ — let’s break this down carefully.</p>
<h3 data-start="54" data-end="96">1. General rule of thumb (small boats)</h3>
<ul data-start="97" data-end="355">
<li data-start="97" data-end="224">
<p data-start="99" data-end="224"><strong data-start="99" data-end="116">Boat capacity</strong> isn’t just about horsepower, it depends on <strong data-start="160" data-end="221">boat length, width (beam), hull design, and weight rating</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="225" data-end="355">
<p data-start="227" data-end="355">The CE/ISO plate on the boat tells you the <strong data-start="270" data-end="318">maximum number of persons + max engine power</strong>. That’s the legal limit in Europe.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="357" data-end="399">2. About a <strong data-start="372" data-end="399">10 HP electric outboard</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="400" data-end="793">
<li data-start="400" data-end="476">
<p data-start="402" data-end="476">A <strong data-start="404" data-end="424">10 HP equivalent</strong> electric motor gives roughly <strong data-start="454" data-end="473">7.5 kW of power</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="477" data-end="541">
<p data-start="479" data-end="541">It’s fine for a small tender (2.5–4 m) or a lightweight RIB.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="542" data-end="647">
<p data-start="544" data-end="647">With that, you can realistically push <strong data-start="582" data-end="608">2–4 adults comfortably</strong> at displacement speeds (~5–7 knots).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="648" data-end="793">
<p data-start="650" data-end="793">If the RIB is bigger (5–6 m, built for 6–8 persons), a 10 HP will <em data-start="716" data-end="722">move</em> it, but only very slowly — like a heavy raft. Not safe or practical.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="795" data-end="821">3. Practical guideline</h3>
<ul data-start="822" data-end="1174">
<li data-start="822" data-end="939">
<p data-start="824" data-end="939"><strong data-start="824" data-end="862">2.4 m dinghy (like your Hercules):</strong> 10 HP is actually more than enough → 2–3 people max, maybe 4 small adults.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="940" data-end="1012">
<p data-start="942" data-end="1012"><strong data-start="942" data-end="958">3.5–4 m RIB:</strong> 10 HP can manage <strong data-start="976" data-end="996">up to 4–5 people</strong> at low speed.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1013" data-end="1174">
<p data-start="1015" data-end="1174"><strong data-start="1015" data-end="1055">5–6 m RIB (the ones used for tours):</strong> designed for 40–100 HP. With only 10 HP, it might carry <strong data-start="1112" data-end="1149">6–7 people but crawl at 2–3 knots</strong>. Unsafe in open water.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1176" data-end="1192">⚠️ Important</h3>
<p data-start="1193" data-end="1387">The <strong data-start="1197" data-end="1224">legal carrying capacity</strong> is set by the manufacturer, not the engine. Even if you put a 10 HP motor on a 6-person RIB, you cannot legally or safely exceed its rated number of passengers.</p>
<hr data-start="1389" data-end="1392">
<p data-start="1394" data-end="1553">👉 In short:<br data-start="1406" data-end="1409">
With a <strong data-start="1416" data-end="1440">10 HP electric motor</strong>, you’re realistically looking at a <strong data-start="1476" data-end="1509">small RIB carrying 2–4 people</strong> comfortably, not a 7-passenger tour boat.</p>
<p data-start="1555" data-end="1708" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to suggest the <strong data-start="1585" data-end="1611">optimal boat size/type</strong> that would work well with a 10 HP electric (so you can maximize passengers without overloading)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10