09C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<hr data-start="1288" data-end="1291">
<h2 data-start="1293" data-end="1330">✅ Where Your Dinghy Beats Big RIBs</h2>
<p data-start="1332" data-end="1405">While you lose out on capacity, speed, and range, you win in other areas:</p>
<ol data-start="1407" data-end="1996">
<li data-start="1407" data-end="1495">
<p data-start="1410" data-end="1495"><strong data-start="1410" data-end="1432">Low operating cost</strong> — cheaper motor, less fuel (if electric), simpler maintenance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1497" data-end="1603">
<p data-start="1500" data-end="1603"><strong data-start="1500" data-end="1526">Lower barrier to entry</strong> — fewer permits, smaller dockage, easier storage, fewer safety requirements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1605" data-end="1736">
<p data-start="1608" data-end="1736"><strong data-start="1608" data-end="1637">Niche, premium experience</strong> — quiet, private, intimate, suited for couples or small groups wanting calm or scenic exploration.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1738" data-end="1885">
<p data-start="1741" data-end="1885"><strong data-start="1741" data-end="1765">Environmental appeal</strong> — especially if electric or low-noise, you can differentiate on eco credentials. Tourists increasingly care about that.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1887" data-end="1996">
<p data-start="1890" data-end="1996"><strong data-start="1890" data-end="1926">Better in confined/narrow places</strong> — caves, coves, shallow water — easier to navigate without big waves.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1998" data-end="2001">
<h2 data-start="2003" data-end="2040">⚠️ Why It Doesn’t Just “Beat” RIBs</h2>
<ul data-start="2042" data-end="2395">
<li data-start="2042" data-end="2183">
<p data-start="2044" data-end="2183">In open water or long distances (like to Paxos), big RIBs are far superior. They can handle choppy seas, higher speed, offshore conditions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2185" data-end="2281">
<p data-start="2187" data-end="2281">Bigger RIBs also carry more people =&gt; economies of scale: revenue per trip can be much higher.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2283" data-end="2395">
<p data-start="2285" data-end="2395">Big RIBs are more visible market participants; many tourists know “boat tour to Paxos” as a premium adventure.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2397" data-end="2400">
<h2 data-start="2402" data-end="2430">🎯 How to Use This Wisely</h2>
<p data-start="2432" data-end="2541">You can’t <em data-start="2442" data-end="2450">outrun</em> the big RIBs in terms of what they do best. But you can <em data-start="2507" data-end="2519">outcompete</em> in a different space:</p>
<ul data-start="2543" data-end="2941">
<li data-start="2543" data-end="2644">
<p data-start="2545" data-end="2644"><strong data-start="2545" data-end="2578">Target local, calm adventures</strong>: caves, coastlines, snorkelling spots rather than long transfers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2646" data-end="2718">
<p data-start="2648" data-end="2718"><strong data-start="2648" data-end="2671">Focus on experience</strong>: quiet, immersive, photographic, eco-friendly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2720" data-end="2782">
<p data-start="2722" data-end="2782"><strong data-start="2722" data-end="2741">Premium pricing</strong> for privacy, uniqueness, views, comfort.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2784" data-end="2941">
<p data-start="2786" data-end="2941"><strong data-start="2786" data-end="2803">Bundle extras</strong> that bigger RIBs won’t offer or can’t offer cheaply: underwater drone video, sunset lighting, marine storytelling, small-group attention.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2943" data-end="2946">
<p data-start="2948" data-end="3137">If you like, I can model a <strong data-start="2975" data-end="3017">side-by-side profit vs cost comparison</strong> between offering a big RIB tour vs your eco-dinghy service, so you can show investors which returns are more realistic?</p>
</div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.