flex flex-col gap-1 px-1"><div class="line-clamp-2 font-medium text-ellipsis text-sm">Quicksilver Air Deck 300 Inflatable RIB 3‑4 Person</div><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex flex-row gap-0.25 text-sm"><div>€1,259.99</div><div class="mx-0.5">•</div><div class="truncate">Waveinn.com</div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute start-0 top-0 flex h-full w-full flex-row"><div class="flex h-full w-9 items-center justify-start opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-100"><button class="btn relative btn-secondary btn-small border-token-border-default active:bg-token-bg-tertiary hover:bg-token-bg-primary h-8 w-8 translate-x-[-50%] rounded-full bg-clip-padding hover:shadow-[0px_4px_16px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05)] active:opacity-100! translate-y-[-85%]"><div class="flex items-center justify-center"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon"><path d="M11.5292 3.7793C11.7889 3.5196 12.211 3.5196 12.4707 3.7793C12.7304 4.039 12.7304 4.461 12.4707 4.7207L7.19136 10L12.4707 15.2793L12.5556 15.3838C12.7261 15.6419 12.6979 15.9934 12.4707 16.2207C12.2434 16.448 11.8919 16.4762 11.6337 16.3057L11.5292 16.2207L5.77925 10.4707C5.51955 10.211 5.51955 9.789 5.77925 9.5293L11.5292 3.7793Z"></path></svg></div></button></div><div class="ms-auto flex h-full w-9 items-center justify-end opacity-100 transition-opacity duration-200"><button class="btn relative btn-secondary btn-small border-token-border-default active:bg-token-bg-tertiary hover:bg-token-bg-primary h-8 w-8 translate-x-[50%] rounded-full bg-clip-padding hover:shadow-[0px_4px_16px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05)] active:opacity-100! translate-y-[-85%]"><div class="flex items-center justify-center"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon"><path d="M7.52925 3.7793C7.75652 3.55203 8.10803 3.52383 8.36616 3.69434L8.47065 3.7793L14.2207 9.5293C14.4804 9.789 14.4804 10.211 14.2207 10.4707L8.47065 16.2207C8.21095 16.4804 7.78895 16.4804 7.52925 16.2207C7.26955 15.961 7.26955 15.539 7.52925 15.2793L12.8085 10L7.52925 4.7207L7.44429 4.61621C7.27378 4.35808 7.30198 4.00657 7.52925 3.7793Z"></path></svg></div></button></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="1278" data-end="1309">Here are some of the top picks:</p>
<ul data-start="1311" data-end="2504">
<li data-start="1311" data-end="1486">
<p data-start="1313" data-end="1486"><strong data-start="1313" data-end="1354"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Zodiac Open 5.5 RIB (~5.5m boat)</span></span></strong>: A full RIB of about 5.5 m — big step up. Likely carries 4-6 people depending on load. Price is high, but very durable and premium.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1488" data-end="1672">
<p data-start="1490" data-end="1672"><strong data-start="1490" data-end="1531"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">VEVOR 6‑Person Inflatable Tender Boat</span></span></strong>: Budget inflatable tender (6 persons nominal) — lighter, less durable than rigid hull, but much lower cost. Good for calm seas / near shore.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1674" data-end="1861">
<p data-start="1676" data-end="1861"><strong data-start="1676" data-end="1717"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Elco EP‑5 Electric 5HP Outboard</span></span></strong>: Electric outboard 5 HP — good for lower loads or as backup. Might be underpowered for full 4-5 persons + gear, but good for 2-3 or calm water.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1863" data-end="1961">
<p data-start="1865" data-end="1961"><strong data-start="1865" data-end="1906"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Epropulsion Elite (~5‑6HP) Electric Outboard</span></span></strong>: Slightly more power; better range. A good mid option.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1963" data-end="2078">
<p data-start="1965" data-end="2078"><strong data-start="1965" data-end="2006"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Rhino VX 34lbs Electric Outboard</span></span></strong>: Strong thrust motor; good torque. Battery cost + weight are important.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2080" data-end="2231">
<p data-start="2082" data-end="2231"><strong data-start="2082" data-end="2125"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">JEENDA 6.5HP (≈4.8kW) Electric Outboard</span></span></strong>: Decent spec for small RIB if you want a “quiet, more eco” feel, though likely needs a good battery bank.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2233" data-end="2365">
<p data-start="2235" data-end="2365"><strong data-start="2235" data-end="2278"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Flipsky 86lbs Electric Outboard Motor</span></span></strong>: More powerful (thrust / weight) — helpful if you want higher speeds or more capacity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2367" data-end="2504">
<p data-start="2369" data-end="2504"><strong data-start="2369" data-end="2412"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Quicksilver Air Deck 300 Inflatable RIB 3‑4 Person</span></span></strong>: Compact RIB, decent for 3-4 people in calm conditions. Lower cost and simpler maintenance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2506" data-end="2509">
<h2 data-start="2511" data-end="2544">✔ Suggested Build / Sweet Spot</h2>
<p data-start="2546" data-end="2647">Here’s what I’d aim for if I were you, to get a good 4-5 person RIB without going into extreme costs:</p>
<ul data-start="2649" data-end="3317">
<li data-start="2649" data-end="2868">
<p data-start="2651" data-end="2868"><strong data-start="2651" data-end="2659">Boat</strong>: ~5 m RIB (rigid or semi-rigid hull, strong tubes, decent beam) — budget used condition is fine, but check for refurbishment needs. Should handle ~400-600 kg gross load (people + gear + motor + battery/fuel).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2869" data-end="3030">
<p data-start="2871" data-end="3030"><strong data-start="2871" data-end="2880">Motor</strong>: ~15-20 HP petrol or ~15-20 kW electric equivalent if budget allows. Electric has higher upfront cost &amp; battery cost, but quieter + marketing appeal.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3031" data-end="3223">
<p data-start="3033" data-end="3223"><strong data-start="3033" data-end="3051">Battery / Fuel</strong>: If electric, invest in battery packs that allow at least 2-3 hours of useful cruising with 4 people (or reserve capacity). If petrol, plan fuel tank + maintenance budget.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3224" data-end="3317">
<p data-start="3226" data-end="3317"><strong data-start="3226" data-end="3236">Extras</strong>: Life jackets, safety gear, minimal shade or cover, perhaps GoPro mount, anchor.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3319" data-end="3322">
<p data-start="3324" data-end="3379">If you want, I can pull together <strong data-start="3357" data-end="3376">two build-plans</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="3380" data-end="3562">
<li data-start="3380" data-end="3448">
<p data-start="3383" data-end="3448"><strong data-start="3383" data-end="3401">“Budget build”</strong> (used RIB + petrol motor) — minimizing cost.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3449" data-end="3562">
<p data-start="3452" data-end="3562"><strong data-start="3452" data-end="3475">“Premium eco build”</strong> (new RIB + electric motor + battery setup) — higher price, higher ticket experience.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="3564" data-end="3585">Would you like those?</p>
