.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="cfebb351-94b4-4994-af66-ced1d8ea9a04" data-testid="conversation-turn-58" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="99246f43-a173-48a8-a6c8-ac3473a10269" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-instant"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="169">That’s a really creative thought ⚡ — using multiple drones (like quadcopters, or underwater thruster modules) as propulsion for a small boat. Let’s look at it seriously:</p>
<hr data-start="171" data-end="174">
<h2 data-start="176" data-end="217">🚤 Can drones be used as boat engines?</h2>
<ul data-start="218" data-end="662">
<li data-start="218" data-end="344">
<p data-start="220" data-end="344"><strong data-start="220" data-end="241">In principle, yes</strong>: propulsion is just pushing water or air. If you mount multiple thrusters on a hull, they can move it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="345" data-end="498">
<p data-start="347" data-end="498">This idea already exists in the form of <strong data-start="387" data-end="415">underwater ROV thrusters</strong> or <strong data-start="419" data-end="447">electric trolling motors</strong> — they’re basically specialized “drones in water.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="499" data-end="662">
<p data-start="501" data-end="662">Aerial drones themselves (quadcopters) aren’t practical for propulsion, but their <strong data-start="583" data-end="616">brushless motors + propellers</strong> are the same tech used in electric thrusters.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="664" data-end="667">
<h2 data-start="669" data-end="692">🔧 How it might work</h2>
<ul data-start="693" data-end="1009">
<li data-start="693" data-end="816">
<p data-start="695" data-end="816">Mount <strong data-start="701" data-end="729">4–6 waterproof thrusters</strong> (like Blue Robotics T200s or cheap Chinese equivalents) on the sides/rear of a dinghy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="817" data-end="879">
<p data-start="819" data-end="879">Control them with a central controller (ESC + battery pack).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="880" data-end="958">
<p data-start="882" data-end="958">They act like a distributed electric outboard: low noise, modular, scalable.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="959" data-end="1009">
<p data-start="961" data-end="1009">If one fails, the others still run → redundancy.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1011" data-end="1014">
<h2 data-start="1016" data-end="1041">📊 Performance reality</h2>
<ul data-start="1042" data-end="1345">
<li data-start="1042" data-end="1121">
<p data-start="1044" data-end="1121">A single ROV thruster (like Blue Robotics T200) gives ~5 kg thrust at 12 V.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1122" data-end="1217">
<p data-start="1124" data-end="1217">To move a 250 kg dinghy with people, you’d need <strong data-start="1172" data-end="1191">40–60 kg thrust</strong> → about 8–12 thrusters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1218" data-end="1298">
<p data-start="1220" data-end="1298">Speed: displacement speeds only (2–4 knots), not planing like a 20 HP motor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1299" data-end="1345">
<p data-start="1301" data-end="1345">Battery drain: huge if you want long runs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1347" data-end="1447">So: it would work, but it would be slow and expensive compared to a single proper electric outboard.</p>
<hr data-start="1449" data-end="1452">
<h2 data-start="1454" data-end="1485">🎯 Where it <em data-start="1469" data-end="1473">is</em> interesting</h2>
<ul data-start="1486" data-end="1755">
<li data-start="1486" data-end="1569">
<p data-start="1488" data-end="1569">As a <strong data-start="1493" data-end="1534">proof-of-concept / futuristic product</strong>: “boat powered by drone swarms.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1570" data-end="1634">
<p data-start="1572" data-end="1634">As an <strong data-start="1578" data-end="1599">eco-tourism angle</strong>: silent, redundant, cool factor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1635" data-end="1755">
<p data-start="1637" data-end="1755">For <strong data-start="1641" data-end="1671">short trips in calm waters</strong> (like Paleokastritsa caves), where speed doesn’t matter but novelty + silence do.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1757" data-end="1760">
<p data-start="1762" data-end="2077">✅ <strong data-start="1764" data-end="1779">Bottom line</strong>:<br data-start="1780" data-end="1783">
Using drones as engines <em data-start="1807" data-end="1817">can work</em>, but it’s more expensive and less efficient than just buying one well-designed electric outboard. Where it could shine is as a <strong data-start="1945" data-end="1992">marketing gimmick and eco-luxury experience</strong> — imagine telling tourists they’re on the <strong data-start="2035" data-end="2075">“first swarm-powered boat in Corfu.”</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2079" data-end="2082">
<p data-start="2084" data-end="2268" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to sketch out a <strong data-start="2115" data-end="2137">modular build plan</strong> (parts list: thrusters, batteries, controller) to see what it would cost to power your 2.4 m dinghy with multiple drone thrusters?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.4