focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="f8fe3d13-fa60-416c-9019-d9c8c37b1d9f" data-testid="conversation-turn-68" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f8fe3d13-fa60-416c-9019-d9c8c37b1d9f" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-instant"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="149">Now that’s a wild idea 🤯 — using <strong data-start="34" data-end="113">underwater drones as the “pull engines” for water skiing or towing a person</strong>. Let’s break it down realistically:</p>
<hr data-start="151" data-end="154">
<h2 data-start="156" data-end="173">⚙️ The physics</h2>
<ul data-start="174" data-end="661">
<li data-start="174" data-end="363">
<p data-start="176" data-end="230"><strong data-start="176" data-end="201">Water skiing / towing</strong> needs <strong data-start="208" data-end="227">a lot of thrust</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="233" data-end="363">
<li data-start="233" data-end="363">
<p data-start="235" data-end="363">Even for a light person, you need ~200–300 kgf of pull (like a 40–100 HP boat engine) just to get them planing on the surface.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="364" data-end="661">
<p data-start="366" data-end="476"><strong data-start="366" data-end="429">Consumer underwater drones (like F1 Pro, Gladius, Hercules)</strong> usually generate <strong data-start="447" data-end="473">2–5 kgf of thrust each</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="479" data-end="661">
<li data-start="479" data-end="536">
<p data-start="481" data-end="536">Even with 10 drones, you’d only have 20–50 kgf total.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="539" data-end="661">
<p data-start="541" data-end="661">That’s enough to tow a GoPro, a small buoy, or a child slowly floating, but not to lift an adult on skis or wakeboard.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="663" data-end="709">So: ❌ <strong data-start="669" data-end="708">not realistic for real water skiing</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="711" data-end="714">
<h2 data-start="716" data-end="748">✅ Where the idea <em data-start="736" data-end="743">could</em> work</h2>
<ol data-start="749" data-end="1485">
<li data-start="749" data-end="1098">
<p data-start="752" data-end="787"><strong data-start="752" data-end="785">Novel “underwater sled” rides</strong></p>
<ul data-start="791" data-end="1098">
<li data-start="791" data-end="889">
<p data-start="793" data-end="889">Instead of pulling someone on skis, you tow a small <strong data-start="845" data-end="870">underwater sled/board</strong> (like a Seabob).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="893" data-end="968">
<p data-start="895" data-end="968">A diver or snorkeler holds on and gets pulled slowly through the water.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="972" data-end="1037">
<p data-start="974" data-end="1037">Speed: 2–3 knots, good for kids, beginners, casual explorers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1041" data-end="1098">
<p data-start="1043" data-end="1098">Drones give direction + stability, not speed thrills.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1100" data-end="1331">
<p data-start="1103" data-end="1130"><strong data-start="1103" data-end="1128">VR/filming experience</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1134" data-end="1331">
<li data-start="1134" data-end="1268">
<p data-start="1136" data-end="1268">Multiple drones film a swimmer/snorkeler from different angles while a tethered underwater scooter provides the actual propulsion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1272" data-end="1331">
<p data-start="1274" data-end="1331">Market as <em data-start="1284" data-end="1329">“cinematic water skiing without the noise.”</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1333" data-end="1485">
<p data-start="1336" data-end="1362"><strong data-start="1336" data-end="1360">Assistive propulsion</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1366" data-end="1485">
<li data-start="1366" data-end="1485">
<p data-start="1368" data-end="1485">Small drones attached to a board/kayak/paddleboard could give a “push” to reduce effort, not a full ski experience.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1487" data-end="1490">
<h2 data-start="1492" data-end="1513">🎯 Marketing angle</h2>
<p data-start="1514" data-end="1556">Instead of <strong data-start="1525" data-end="1541">water skiing</strong>, sell it as:</p>
<p data-start="1558" data-end="1717">👉 <em data-start="1561" data-end="1582">“Underwater Flight”</em> – Guests hold onto a handlebar connected to tethered drones, and they <strong data-start="1653" data-end="1687">glide slowly through the water</strong> while watching marine life.</p>
<ul data-start="1719" data-end="1847">
<li data-start="1719" data-end="1742">
<p data-start="1721" data-end="1742">Safe, eco, and fun.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1743" data-end="1784">
<p data-start="1745" data-end="1784">Works for kids, families, non-skiers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1785" data-end="1847">
<p data-start="1787" data-end="1847">Easy to integrate with your existing F1 Pro/Hercules gear.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1849" data-end="1852">
<p data-start="1854" data-end="2017">⚡ <strong data-start="1856" data-end="1871">Bottom line</strong>:<br data-start="1872" data-end="1875">
Drones can’t deliver enough power for “skiing,” but they <em data-start="1932" data-end="1937">can</em> create a <strong data-start="1947" data-end="1986">gentle, futuristic glide experience</strong> that no speedboat can offer.</p>
<hr data-start="2019" data-end="2022">
<p data-start="2024" data-end="2202" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to sketch a <strong data-start="2051" data-end="2102">prototype design for an “underwater glide sled”</strong> (handlebar + multiple drones pulling a person horizontally) that you could actually build and test?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3