17.2386 3.56261 17.2031L3.41417 17.1543C3.19115 17.0586 3.00741 16.8908 2.89171 16.6797L2.84581 16.5859C2.75951 16.3846 2.76168 16.1912 2.7716 16.0596C2.7813 15.931 2.80736 15.7796 2.83117 15.6367L3.2296 13.2432L3.36437 12.4785C3.40893 12.2616 3.45789 12.0745 3.52453 11.8926L3.6173 11.6621C3.71685 11.4352 3.83766 11.2176 3.97765 11.0127L4.15343 10.7783C4.34386 10.5462 4.58164 10.312 4.90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="c943261c-7757-4d6a-ba94-6e3c586ff4d1" data-testid="conversation-turn-80" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="c943261c-7757-4d6a-ba94-6e3c586ff4d1" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-instant"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="137">Great, let’s dive into the <strong data-start="27" data-end="56">Underwater Tow Experience</strong> idea 🌊🤖 — it’s very different from boats, but it has strong novelty potential.</p>
<hr data-start="139" data-end="142">
<h2 data-start="144" data-end="166">🎯 The Core Concept</h2>
<ul data-start="167" data-end="449">
<li data-start="167" data-end="236">
<p data-start="169" data-end="236">Instead of water skiing, guests <strong data-start="201" data-end="233">hold onto a handlebar / sled</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="237" data-end="307">
<p data-start="239" data-end="307">Multiple <strong data-start="248" data-end="286">underwater drones pull them slowly</strong> through the water.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="308" data-end="382">
<p data-start="310" data-end="382">The guest “flies” underwater — like scuba diving, but with propulsion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="383" data-end="449">
<p data-start="385" data-end="449">Safe, silent, eco-friendly alternative to jet skis or Seabobs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="451" data-end="454">
<h2 data-start="456" data-end="481">⚙️ Technical Breakdown</h2>
<ul data-start="482" data-end="998">
<li data-start="482" data-end="552">
<p data-start="484" data-end="552"><strong data-start="484" data-end="494">Drones</strong>: your F1 Pro + others can produce ~2–3 kgf thrust each.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="553" data-end="705">
<p data-start="555" data-end="575"><strong data-start="555" data-end="572">Pull strength</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="578" data-end="705">
<li data-start="578" data-end="653">
<p data-start="580" data-end="653">2 drones = gentle towing for a child or light adult (snorkeling speed).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="656" data-end="705">
<p data-start="658" data-end="705">3–4 drones = more fun, adult-level “gliding.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="706" data-end="783">
<p data-start="708" data-end="783"><strong data-start="708" data-end="717">Speed</strong>: ~2–3 knots → enough to feel movement, but safe for snorkelers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="784" data-end="927">
<p data-start="786" data-end="800"><strong data-start="786" data-end="797">Control</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="803" data-end="927">
<li data-start="803" data-end="871">
<p data-start="805" data-end="871">Drones could be tethered to a <strong data-start="835" data-end="847">sled bar</strong> that the guest holds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="874" data-end="927">
<p data-start="876" data-end="927">Operator on surface (staff) controls power/speed.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="928" data-end="998">
<p data-start="930" data-end="998"><strong data-start="930" data-end="940">Safety</strong>: Always tethered to floating base/boat, so no drifting.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1000" data-end="1003">
<h2 data-start="1005" data-end="1026">🧩 Experience Flow</h2>
<ol data-start="1027" data-end="1300">
<li data-start="1027" data-end="1078">
<p data-start="1030" data-end="1078">Guest wears mask/snorkel (or small scuba set).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1079" data-end="1137">
<p data-start="1082" data-end="1137">They hold onto the sled/handlebar attached to drones.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1138" data-end="1178">
<p data-start="1141" data-end="1178">Staff guides drones slowly forward.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1179" data-end="1249">
<p data-start="1182" data-end="1249">Guest glides over reefs, caves, fish — hands free, no fin effort.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1250" data-end="1300">
<p data-start="1253" data-end="1300">Drone cameras film the ride → souvenir video.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1302" data-end="1305">
<h2 data-start="1307" data-end="1322">✅ Advantages</h2>
<ul data-start="1323" data-end="1603">
<li data-start="1323" data-end="1388">
<p data-start="1325" data-end="1388"><strong data-start="1325" data-end="1335">Unique</strong>: feels futuristic; no one else in Corfu offers it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1389" data-end="1478">
<p data-start="1391" data-end="1478"><strong data-start="1391" data-end="1404">Inclusive</strong>: suitable for kids, non-swimmers (with life vest + snorkel at surface).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1479" data-end="1532">
<p data-start="1481" data-end="1532"><strong data-start="1481" data-end="1488">Eco</strong>: no noisy engines, no bubbles like scuba.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1533" data-end="1603">
<p data-start="1535" data-end="1603"><strong data-start="1535" data-end="1551">Cheap luxury</strong>: uses equipment you partly already have (drones).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1605" data-end="1608">
<h2 data-start="1610" data-end="1633">💶 Pricing Potential</h2>
<ul data-start="1634" data-end="1807">
<li data-start="1634" data-end="1673">
<p data-start="1636" data-end="1673"><strong data-start="1636" data-end="1670">€40–60 per session (15–20 min)</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1674" data-end="1732">
<p data-start="1676" data-end="1732">Works well as an add-on to your Floating Base product.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1733" data-end="1807">
<p data-start="1735" data-end="1807">With 10–12 guests per day → €400–600/day gross just from towing rides.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1809" data-end="1812">
<h2 data-start="1814" data-end="1835">🔧 Prototype Build</h2>
<ul data-start="1836" data-end="2027">
<li data-start="1836" data-end="1928">
<p data-start="1838" data-end="1928"><strong data-start="1838" data-end="1850">Tow sled</strong>: lightweight plastic/fiberglass handlebar frame with mounts for 2–4 drones.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1929" data-end="1968">
<p data-start="1931" data-end="1968"><strong data-start="1931" data-end="1954">Quick-release clips</strong> for safety.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1969" data-end="2027">
<p data-start="1971" data-end="2027"><strong data-start="1971" data-end="1994">Surface tether line</strong> for recovery if a drone fails.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2029" data-end="2032">
<p data-start="2034" data-end="2172">⚡ Imagine the marketing: <em data-start="2059" data-end="2102">“Fly Underwater with the Power of Drones”</em>.<br data-start="2103" data-end="2106">
It’s like scuba + jet ski + VR all combined, but cheaper to run.</p>
<p data-start="2174" data-end="2287" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">👉 Do you want me to <strong data-start="2195" data-end="2251">sketch a design for the tow-sled with mounted drones</strong>, like I did with the floating base?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 