<p data-start="289" data-end="322">Here are some of the top options:</p>
<ul data-start="324" data-end="1177">
<li data-start="324" data-end="455">
<p data-start="326" data-end="455"><strong data-start="326" data-end="367"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">IPX8 2.4 kg Underwater Thruster (~€66)</span></span></strong>: Cheap, lightweight, good for testing. Might be underpowered if you need strong pull.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="456" data-end="564">
<p data-start="458" data-end="564"><strong data-start="458" data-end="499"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">14.2 kg Thrust Aluminium Thruster (~€850)</span></span></strong>: Stronger thrust, good if you want decent power from each end.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="565" data-end="673">
<p data-start="567" data-end="673"><strong data-start="567" data-end="608"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">BlueRobotics T200 Thruster (~€230)</span></span></strong>: Very solid choice; reliable brand, good community, good spec.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="674" data-end="781">
<p data-start="676" data-end="781"><strong data-start="676" data-end="717"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">CubeMars SW7 360 W Thruster (~€324)</span></span></strong>: Mid-power, good for a balanced dual-motor paddle end system.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="783" data-end="875">
<p data-start="785" data-end="875"><strong data-start="785" data-end="826"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">EcoWorthy 12 V 100 Ah LiFePO4 Bat (~€372)</span></span></strong>: Good quality battery, “middle size” capacity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="876" data-end="979">
<p data-start="878" data-end="979"><strong data-start="878" data-end="919"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Renogy 12 V 200 Ah LiFePO4 (~€441)</span></span></strong>: Larger capacity; heavier, more costly, but more runtime.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="980" data-end="1068">
<p data-start="982" data-end="1068"><strong data-start="982" data-end="1023"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">WattCycle 12 V 314 Ah LiFePO4 (~€530)</span></span></strong>: Big battery, gives more runtime, heavier.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1069" data-end="1177">
<p data-start="1071" data-end="1177"><strong data-start="1071" data-end="1112"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Victron 12.8 V 50 Ah Smart LiFePO4 (~€452)</span></span></strong>: Smaller capacity but from a very trusted brand; smart features.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1179" data-end="1182">
