<p data-start="1270" data-end="1295">Here are a few standouts:</p>
<ul data-start="1297" data-end="1844">
<li data-start="1297" data-end="1468">
<p data-start="1299" data-end="1468"><strong data-start="1299" data-end="1340"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">ApisQueen U2‑Set 300 W Thruster</span></span></strong> — 300 W, quite good thrust, probably in range of ~10-12 kgf (just guessing). This could be used at ends of paddle for 2 people.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1470" data-end="1603">
<p data-start="1472" data-end="1603"><strong data-start="1472" data-end="1513"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">IPX8 2.4 kg Underwater Thruster</span></span></strong> — lightweight, below what you need alone, but could serve for lighter loads or test runs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1605" data-end="1716">
<p data-start="1607" data-end="1716"><strong data-start="1607" data-end="1648"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">CubeMars SW7 360 W Thruster</span></span></strong> — great mid-power; possibly a good balance vs weight + energy draw.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1718" data-end="1844">
<p data-start="1720" data-end="1844"><strong data-start="1720" data-end="1761"><span class="entity-underline hover:entity-accent inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Savage Gear&nbsp;55 lbs Thruster</span></span></strong> — this is quite powerful; might overshoot the needed thrust, but gives you margin.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1846" data-end="1849">
<h2 data-start="1851" data-end="1934">✅ My picks for your application (Aqua Marina Beta 312, 2 people, 1-hour battery)</h2>
<p data-start="1936" data-end="2009">To get ~30-40 lbs thrust combined (i.e. ~15-20 kgf), supporting 2 people:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="2011" data-end="2723" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2011" data-end="2069"><tr data-start="2011" data-end="2069"><th data-start="2011" data-end="2027" data-col-size="sm">Configuration</th><th data-start="2027" data-end="2041" data-col-size="md">Thruster(s)</th><th data-start="2041" data-end="2056" data-col-size="md">Why it works</th><th data-start="2056" data-end="2069" data-col-size="md">Tradeoffs</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2088" data-end="2723"><tr data-start="2088" data-end="2283"><td data-start="2088" data-end="2118" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2090" data-end="2117">Balanced dual thrusters</strong></td><td data-start="2118" data-end="2153" data-col-size="md">2 × ApisQueen U92 (~20 lbs each)</td><td data-start="2153" data-end="2227" data-col-size="md">Combined ~40 lbs, good match vs current &amp; weight; manageable power draw</td><td data-start="2227" data-end="2283" data-col-size="md">Needs good battery; sealing + wiring for both motors</td></tr><tr data-start="2284" data-end="2503"><td data-start="2284" data-end="2316" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2286" data-end="2315">One strong + one moderate</strong></td><td data-start="2316" data-end="2362" data-col-size="md">One Savage Gear 55 lbs + one modest ~20 lbs</td><td data-start="2362" data-end="2429" data-col-size="md">Strong power reserve; can use both or single motor in calm water</td><td data-start="2429" data-end="2503" data-col-size="md">Heavier, more expensive; risk of being overpowered in light conditions</td></tr><tr data-start="2504" data-end="2723"><td data-start="2504" data-end="2540" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2506" data-end="2539">High-capacity mid-power setup</strong></td><td data-start="2540" data-end="2565" data-col-size="md">2 × CubeMars SW7 360 W</td><td data-start="2565" data-end="2654" data-col-size="md">Enough power; likely good balance of wattage &amp; thrust for renting; higher cost upfront</td><td data-start="2654" data-end="2723" data-col-size="md">Battery size &amp; cost will increase; weight of thrusters &gt;2 kg each</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 32.8906px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 