-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="56">Yes 👍 I remember — you’re running a <strong data-start="37" data-end="53">hybrid setup</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="58" data-end="201">
<li data-start="58" data-end="124">
<p data-start="60" data-end="124"><strong data-start="60" data-end="72">Frontend</strong>: Static Next.js export hosted at <strong data-start="106" data-end="121">Creta Force</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="125" data-end="201">
<p data-start="127" data-end="201"><strong data-start="127" data-end="138">Backend</strong>: Custom <strong data-start="147" data-end="162">Node.js app</strong>, hosted separately (Render, right?).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="203" data-end="282">This is exactly the same approach you used for your hotel / booking projects.</p>
<p data-start="284" data-end="340">So for <strong data-start="291" data-end="304">IonianEMS</strong>, you can follow the same pattern:</p>
<hr data-start="342" data-end="345">
<h2 data-start="347" data-end="386">⚙️ Hybrid Architecture for IonianEMS</h2>
<ol data-start="387" data-end="1048">
<li data-start="387" data-end="594">
<p data-start="390" data-end="416"><strong data-start="390" data-end="416">Frontend (Creta Force)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="420" data-end="594">
<li data-start="420" data-end="488">
<p data-start="422" data-end="488">Static Next.js site for marketing, dashboards, and public pages.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="492" data-end="530">
<p data-start="494" data-end="530">Fast, SEO-friendly, easy to scale.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="534" data-end="594">
<p data-start="536" data-end="594">Multi-language ready (Greek, English, German if needed).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="596" data-end="858">
<p data-start="599" data-end="620"><strong data-start="599" data-end="620">Backend (Node.js)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="624" data-end="858">
<li data-start="624" data-end="683">
<p data-start="626" data-end="683">Handles real-time data ingestion from sensors / drones.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="687" data-end="731">
<p data-start="689" data-end="731">Exposes REST or GraphQL API to frontend.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="735" data-end="804">
<p data-start="737" data-end="804">Stores data in MongoDB or PostgreSQL (Render, Atlas, or similar).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="808" data-end="858">
<p data-start="810" data-end="858">WebSocket layer for live alerts / map updates.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="860" data-end="1048">
<p data-start="863" data-end="879"><strong data-start="863" data-end="879">Integrations</strong></p>
<ul data-start="883" data-end="1048">
<li data-start="883" data-end="929">
<p data-start="885" data-end="929">AIS / weather data feeds (3rd party APIs).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="933" data-end="987">
<p data-start="935" data-end="987">Drone telemetry (video streams, object detection).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="991" data-end="1048">
<p data-start="993" data-end="1048">EMS features (alerts, geofencing, emergency contact).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1050" data-end="1053">
<h2 data-start="1055" data-end="1097">🚀 Why this hybrid model fits IonianEMS</h2>
<ul data-start="1098" data-end="1395">
<li data-start="1098" data-end="1155">
<p data-start="1100" data-end="1155">Keeps <strong data-start="1106" data-end="1130">frontend lightweight</strong> for SEO and marketing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1156" data-end="1237">
<p data-start="1158" data-end="1237">Backend is <strong data-start="1169" data-end="1181">flexible</strong> for real-time, heavy processing (AI vision, mapping).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1238" data-end="1333">
<p data-start="1240" data-end="1333">Easy to scale: frontend for 1,000s of visitors, backend for fewer but data-intensive users.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1334" data-end="1395">
<p data-start="1336" data-end="1395">Lower hosting cost (Creta Force static + Render backend).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1397" data-end="1400">
<p data-start="1402" data-end="1611" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">👉 Question for you:<br data-start="1422" data-end="1425">
For IonianEMS, do you want to first focus on the <strong data-start="1474" data-end="1506">tourist-facing “wow” product</strong> (like interactive maps, drone visuals), or on the <strong data-start="1557" data-end="1581">serious EMS features</strong> (alerts, safety for boaters)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 1