</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="906" data-end="958">→ it will return the actual file instead of a 404.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="960" data-end="963">
<p data-start="965" data-end="1237">⚠️ Important: On <strong data-start="982" data-end="1003">Azure App Service</strong>, the <code data-start="1009" data-end="1019">/uploads</code> folder must exist in your deployed backend. If your upload code saves files locally, make sure you’re deploying with <code data-start="1137" data-end="1147">/uploads</code> included, or switch to cloud storage (like Azure Blob Storage) if you need persistence.</p>
