</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
</li>
<li data-start="1322" data-end="1374">
<p data-start="1324" data-end="1374">Commit &amp; deploy → Azure will now serve <code data-start="1363" data-end="1373">/uploads</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1376" data-end="1379">
<h2 data-start="1381" data-end="1399">⚡ Long-term fix</h2>
<p data-start="1400" data-end="1447">For production, don’t rely on local <code data-start="1436" data-end="1446">/uploads</code>:</p>
<ul data-start="1448" data-end="1655">
<li data-start="1448" data-end="1549">
<p data-start="1450" data-end="1549">Configure your <code data-start="1465" data-end="1482">uploadRoutes.js</code> to upload to <strong data-start="1496" data-end="1510">Cloudinary</strong> (you already have API keys in <code data-start="1541" data-end="1547">.env</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1550" data-end="1581">
<p data-start="1552" data-end="1581">Or to <strong data-start="1558" data-end="1580">Azure Blob Storage</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1582" data-end="1655">
<p data-start="1584" data-end="1655">Then store the <strong data-start="1599" data-end="1617">full image URL</strong> in MongoDB instead of <code data-start="1640" data-end="1654">/uploads/...</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1657" data-end="1660">
