-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="113">Got it 👍 let’s troubleshoot step by step.<br data-start="42" data-end="45">
Here’s <strong data-start="52" data-end="69">what to check</strong> to solve the missing product image problem:</p>
<hr data-start="115" data-end="118">
<h3 data-start="120" data-end="179">1️⃣ Check if the <code data-start="141" data-end="151">/uploads</code> folder exists on the server</h3>
<ul data-start="180" data-end="378">
<li data-start="180" data-end="239">
<p data-start="182" data-end="239">Go to your backend project root (locally and on Azure).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="240" data-end="284">
<p data-start="242" data-end="284">Is there an <code data-start="254" data-end="264">/uploads</code> folder inside it?</p>
</li>
<li data-start="285" data-end="308">
<p data-start="287" data-end="308">If not → create it.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="309" data-end="378">
<p data-start="311" data-end="378">Add an empty file (<code data-start="330" data-end="340">.gitkeep</code>) so GitHub/Azure doesn’t ignore it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="380" data-end="383">
<h3 data-start="385" data-end="431">2️⃣ Check if Express is serving the folder</h3>
<p data-start="432" data-end="449">You already have:</p>
