</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="244" data-end="247">
<h3 data-start="249" data-end="272">🔍 Why this happens</h3>
<p data-start="273" data-end="519">You’re hosting on <strong data-start="291" data-end="306">Creta Force</strong> (static Next.js export).<br data-start="331" data-end="334">
With <code data-start="339" data-end="352">next export</code>, all routes must be <strong data-start="373" data-end="404">pre-generated at build time</strong>.<br data-start="405" data-end="408">
Dynamic routes like <code data-start="428" data-end="443">/product/[id]</code> don’t exist as HTML files in the static build → so nginx can’t find them.</p>
<p data-start="521" data-end="594">That’s why it works locally (<code data-start="550" data-end="563">npm run dev</code>) but not on the deployed site.</p>
<hr data-start="596" data-end="599">
<h3 data-start="601" data-end="618">✅ Fix options</h3>
<ol data-start="620" data-end="1461">
<li data-start="620" data-end="886">
<p data-start="623" data-end="667"><strong data-start="623" data-end="653">Switch to query param URLs</strong> (static safe)</p>
<ul data-start="671" data-end="886">
<li data-start="671" data-end="783">
<p data-start="673" data-end="718">Instead of <code data-start="684" data-end="706">/product/68d3b4dc...</code>, link to:</p>
