2 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-68d18f8a-0424-832f-8f72-1abe7912afa2-11" data-testid="conversation-turn-172" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant" style=""><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="e6e4ad9a-b4c5-4ecc-8a67-873f75335550" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="31">Yes ✅ that makes total sense.</p>
<p data-start="33" data-end="88">Here’s why it works <strong data-start="53" data-end="64">locally</strong> but fails <strong data-start="75" data-end="85">online</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="90" data-end="637">
<li data-start="90" data-end="365">
<p data-start="92" data-end="156"><strong data-start="92" data-end="119">Locally (<code data-start="103" data-end="116">npm run dev</code>)</strong> → Next.js runs a real Node server.</p>
<ul data-start="159" data-end="365">
<li data-start="159" data-end="295">
<p data-start="161" data-end="295">When you open <code data-start="175" data-end="210">/product/68d3b4dc2cc0ae544c6ad373</code>, the server calls your API (<code data-start="239" data-end="258">/api/products/:id</code>) and renders the page dynamically.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="298" data-end="365">
<p data-start="300" data-end="365">That’s why new products show up immediately without rebuilding.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="367" data-end="637">
<p data-start="369" data-end="448"><strong data-start="369" data-end="409">Online (Creta Force + <code data-start="393" data-end="406">next export</code>)</strong> → You’re serving a <strong data-start="429" data-end="445">static build</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="451" data-end="637">
<li data-start="451" data-end="540">
<p data-start="453" data-end="540"><code data-start="453" data-end="466">next export</code> pre-builds HTML files only for the products that existed at build time.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="543" data-end="637">
<p data-start="545" data-end="637">When you add a new product later, no HTML exists for it, so nginx returns <code data-start="619" data-end="634">404 Not Found</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="639" data-end="644">So:</p>
<ul data-start="645" data-end="721">
<li data-start="645" data-end="682">
<p data-start="647" data-end="682"><strong data-start="647" data-end="680">Local = dynamic server render</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="683" data-end="721">
<p data-start="685" data-end="721"><strong data-start="685" data-end="719">Production = static files only</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="723" data-end="726">
<h3 data-start="728" data-end="758">✅ Your choices to fix this</h3>
<ol data-start="760" data-end="1698">
<li data-start="760" data-end="960">
<p data-start="763" data-end="798"><strong data-start="763" data-end="796">Rebuild after adding products</strong></p>
<ul data-start="802" data-end="960">
<li data-start="802" data-end="883">
<p data-start="804" data-end="883">Each time you add a product, re-run <code data-start="840" data-end="867">next build &amp;&amp; next export</code> and redeploy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="887" data-end="929">
<p data-start="889" data-end="929">This regenerates static product pages.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="933" data-end="960">
<p data-start="935" data-end="960">Works, but it’s annoying.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="962" data-end="1307">
<p data-start="965" data-end="1016"><strong data-start="965" data-end="1014">Switch product detail to Client-Side Fetching</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1020" data-end="1307">
<li data-start="1020" data-end="1156">
<p data-start="1022" data-end="1156">Instead of relying on prebuilt HTML, make your <code data-start="1069" data-end="1078">[id].js</code> page fetch the product data via API at runtime (<code data-start="1127" data-end="1138">useEffect</code> + Axios/Fetch).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1160" data-end="1220">
<p data-start="1162" data-end="1220">Then even new products added after deployment will work.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1224" data-end="1307">
<p data-start="1226" data-end="1307">Downside: SEO isn’t as strong because the HTML is mostly empty until React loads.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1309" data-end="1698">
<p data-start="1312" data-end="1364"><strong data-start="1312" data-end="1331">Hybrid approach</strong> (best practice if SEO matters)</p>
<ul data-start="1368" data-end="1698">
<li data-start="1368" data-end="1429">
<p data-start="1370" data-end="1429">Use <code data-start="1374" data-end="1390">getStaticPaths</code> for popular products (pre-rendered).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1433" data-end="1565">
<p data-start="1435" data-end="1565">Add <code data-start="1439" data-end="1461">fallback: 'blocking'</code> → so if a product page doesn’t exist yet, Next.js generates it on demand the first time it’s visited.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1569" data-end="1698">
<p data-start="1571" data-end="1698">⚠️ BUT: <code data-start="1579" data-end="1589">fallback</code> does <strong data-start="1595" data-end="1602">not</strong> work with <code data-start="1613" data-end="1626">next export</code> (static export). You’d need a real Next.js server (Vercel, Node, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1700" data-end="1703">
<p data-start="1705" data-end="1802">👉 Since you’re on <strong data-start="1724" data-end="1758">Creta Force with static export</strong>, your <strong data-start="1765" data-end="1795">only two realistic options</strong> are:</p>
<ul data-start="1803" data-end="1922">
<li data-start="1803" data-end="1847">
<p data-start="1805" data-end="1847">Rebuild on every new product (option 1).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1848" data-end="1922">
<p data-start="1850" data-end="1922">Or switch product detail pages to <strong data-start="1884" data-end="1908">client-side fetching</strong> (option 2).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1924" data-end="1927">
<p data-start="1929" data-end="2076" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to rewrite your product page so it works with <strong data-start="1990" data-end="2014">client-side fetching</strong> (option 2), meaning you can add products without redeploying?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V1