</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="186" data-end="334">But your frontend was still treating them as if they were <strong data-start="244" data-end="274">local <code data-start="252" data-end="266">/uploads/...</code> files</strong>, so it prepended your backend domain. That’s why you saw:</p>
