styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="109">Ahh ✅ thanks for clarifying — so originally the <strong data-start="48" data-end="75">page itself loaded fine</strong>, only the <strong data-start="86" data-end="95">image</strong> was broken.</p>
<p data-start="111" data-end="130">That makes sense:</p>
<ul data-start="131" data-end="343">
<li data-start="131" data-end="226">
<p data-start="133" data-end="226">The <code data-start="137" data-end="158">404 Not Found nginx</code> you saw earlier was from <strong data-start="184" data-end="201">the image URL</strong>, not the product page.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="227" data-end="343">
<p data-start="229" data-end="343">After you reverted your <code data-start="253" data-end="262">&lt;Image&gt;</code> logic, the <strong data-start="274" data-end="282">page</strong> works again, but sometimes the image path handling is wrong.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="345" data-end="348">
<h3 data-start="350" data-end="370">Why this happens</h3>
<ul data-start="371" data-end="532">
<li data-start="371" data-end="448">
<p data-start="373" data-end="448">Old products (before Cloudinary) → <code data-start="408" data-end="445">product.image = "/uploads/xxx.webp"</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="449" data-end="532">
<p data-start="451" data-end="532">New products (Cloudinary) → <code data-start="479" data-end="529">product.image = "https://res.cloudinary.com/..."</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="534" data-end="552">Your current code:</p>
