rose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="88">Yes ✅ that’s completely normal when you open an <strong data-start="48" data-end="55">SVG</strong> file directly in your browser.</p>
<p data-start="90" data-end="262">SVG is an XML-based vector graphic format, so the browser just renders it as an image — but if you open it in a text/tab view, it looks like XML and you’ll see the message:</p>
