2" data-end="93">use a public link</strong> where the image is already hosted and you can right-click → <em data-start="154" data-end="163">Save As</em>.</p>
<p data-start="168" data-end="212">Here’s a clean PNG placeholder you can grab:</p>
<p data-start="214" data-end="327">📥 <strong data-start="217" data-end="262">Right-click → Save As → <code data-start="243" data-end="260">placeholder.png</code></strong><br data-start="262" data-end="265">
👉 <a data-start="268" data-end="327" rel="noopener" target="_new" class="decorated-link cursor-pointer">Download placeholder.png<span aria-hidden="true" class="ms-0.5 inline-block align-middle leading-none"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" data-rtl-flip="" class="block h-[0.75em] w-[0.75em] stroke-current stroke-[0.75]"><path d="M14.3349 13.3301V6.60645L5.47065 15.4707C5.21095 15.7304 4.78895 15.7304 4.52925 15.4707C4.26955 15.211 4.26955 14.789 4.52925 14.5293L13.3935 5.66504H6.66011C6.29284 5.66504 5.99507 5.36727 5.99507 5C5.99507 4.63273 6.29284 4.33496 6.66011 4.33496H14.9999L15.1337 4.34863C15.4369 4.41057 15.665 4.67857 15.665 5V13.3301C15.6649 13.6973 15.3672 13.9951 14.9999 13.9951C14.6327 13.9951 14.335 13.6973 14.3349 13.3301Z"></path></svg></span></a></p>
<p data-start="329" data-end="393">It looks like a neutral grey box with text “No Image Available”.</p>
<hr data-start="395" data-end="398">
<h3 data-start="400" data-end="417">How to use it</h3>
